  "caption": "Cantonese pop built almost entirely from voices. Vocal percussion providing the entire drum part with mouth-made kick, snare and hi-hat sounds, stacked human voices singing the harmonic bed in close four-part blocks, hummed pads underneath, and one upright bass as the only instrument. Close and warm with the voices layered densely and only light plate reverb. Lead female voice sitting on top of the ensemble, conversational and clear, with the group answering her lines. 92 BPM, A major. Counting how many people once thought of you. No drum kit, no synth, no guitars, no piano, no key change.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n雪櫃門 貼咗十九塊磁石\n冇一塊係我自己買嘅\n全部都係人哋去完旅行 順手買返嚟畀我\n大阪 清邁 台中 首爾 有塊寫住「蘇梅島」 我唔記得邊個\n\n[Chorus]\n雪櫃上面嘅磁石\n十九個人 唔同時間 唔同地方\n諗起過我一次\n一次就夠 一次已經貼咗喺度好多年\n\n[Verse]\n搬屋嗰陣 搬運師傅問我「呢啲要唔要」\n我話要 佢望我 我都知自己好煩\n我逐塊撕落嚟 用報紙包住\n包一塊磁石 我自己都覺得自己癲\n\n[Chorus]\n雪櫃上面嘅磁石\n十九個人 唔同時間 唔同地方\n諗起過我一次\n一次就夠 而家佢哋貼咗喺新屋\n\n[Outro]\n新雪櫃大啲\n仲有位",
